.TH ONEC 1 "March 2026" "OpenNEC" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
onec \- antenna simulation tool using the NEC-2 method-of-moments engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onec
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIFILE\fR .\|.\|.\|]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B onec
is the command-line interface to OpenNEC, an implementation of the
Numerical Electromagnetics Code (NEC-2) antenna modelling engine.
It reads one or more antenna-design decks (plain-text files of
geometry and control cards), runs the requested electromagnetic
simulations, and writes the results.
.PP
A single deck describes the physical layout of an antenna (wire
segments, surfaces, loads, and ground parameters) together with the
simulation controls (frequency sweeps, excitations, and output
requests).  The canonical file extension is
.B .nec
or
.BR .deck .
.PP
Multiple input files or directories may be given on the command line.
When more than one input is processed,
.B onec
writes each result to a sidecar file named
.IB input .out
next to the source file, and uses
.I stdout
to report progress.  With a single input and no
.B \-o
flag, results go to
.IR stdout .
.PP
If no file is given at all, the deck is read from
.IR stdin .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Recurse into subdirectories when a directory is given as an argument.
By default only files whose extensions are recognised as NEC decks
.RI ( .nec ,
.IR .deck )
are processed.  Combine with a quoted glob to select a different
extension (see
.B EXAMPLES
below).
.TP
.BR \-\-skip\-large
When running a batch of files, files whose estimated complexity T is \(ge 1e11 are skipped.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-run
Parse and validate the deck but do not execute the simulation.
Often combined with
.B \-t
to perform a quick syntax check.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test\-deck
Run built-in deck sanity checks and report any warnings or errors.
Can be combined with
.B \-n
to check without simulating.
.TP
.BI \-i " file" "\fR,\fP \-\-input\-file=" file
Read the deck from
.IR file .
This flag is not required; a bare positional argument has the same
effect and takes precedence if both are given.
.TP
.BI \-o " file" "\fR,\fP \-\-output\-file=" file
Write simulation results to
.IR file .
With a single input and no
.B \-o
flag the results go to
.IR stdout .
With multiple inputs or
.BR \-r ,
output is always written to per-file
.I .out
sidecar files regardless of this flag.
Passing
.B \-o
with no argument (or with just
.BR \- )
forces output to
.IR stdout .
.TP
.BI \-e " file" "\fR,\fP \-\-error\-file=" file
Redirect error and diagnostic messages to
.I file
instead of
.IR stderr .
.TP
.BI \-g\fR[\fIfile\fR] ", " \-\-greens\fR[=\fIfile\fR]
Compute and write a Green's function file.  The filename defaults to
the input path with the extension replaced by
.BR .ngf .
.TP
.BI \-j " N" "\fR,\fP \-\-jobs=" N
When processing multiple input files, run up to
.I N
simulations in parallel.  Defaults to
.BR 1 .
.TP
.BI \-w " file" "\fR,\fP \-\-write\-file=" file
Convert and write the deck to
.I file
in the format inferred from its extension.
Pass a bare extension such as
.B .maa
to convert multiple input files in-place (each output is written next
to its corresponding input file).
Supported output formats: see
.B FILE FORMATS
below.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format
Select the output format for generated
.IR .out
files.  Valid values are
.B nec2c
for the modern Unix-style output layout, and
.B original
for the classic Fortran-style layout.
The default is
.B nec2c
on Unix and
.B original
on Windows.
.PP
Single-letter flags that take no argument may be combined:
.B \-nt
is equivalent to
.BR "\-n \-t" .
.SH FILE FORMATS
.B onec
recognises the following file formats.
.TS
l l l l.
\fBExtension(s)\fP	\fBFormat\fP	\fBRead\fP	\fBWrite\fP
_
\fI.nec\fP, \fI.deck\fP, \fI.4nec\fP	OpenNEC / NEC-2 deck	yes	yes
\fI.nec2\fP	NEC-2 stripped numeric	yes	yes
\fI.nec4\fP	NEC-4	yes	stub
\fI.maa\fP, \fI.mma\fP	MMANA-GAL	yes	yes
\fI.yo\fP, \fI.ant\fP, \fI.yag\fP	Yagi Optimizer	yes	yes
\fI.ez\fP, \fI.ezn\fP	EZNEC	detected	\(em
\fI.nwp\fP, \fI.nwz\fP	NEC-Win Plus/Zip	detected	\(em
\fI.aci\fP	AntSolver	detected	\(em
\fI.mmae\fP	MMANA-EZ	detected	\(em
.TE
.PP
\(lqDetected\(rq means the extension is recognised and a helpful error
is shown, but no converter exists yet.  When a directory is scanned
with
.BR \-r ,
only NEC deck extensions are collected automatically; all other formats
must be passed explicitly or with a glob pattern.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a simulation and print results to stdout:
.PP
.RS
.B onec example.nec
.RE
.PP
Run a simulation and write results to the default sidecar file
.IR example.out :
.PP
.RS
.B onec \-o example.nec
.RE
.PP
Run a simulation and write results to a named file:
.PP
.RS
.B onec \-o result.out example.nec
.RE
.PP
Parse and validate a deck without simulating:
.PP
.RS
.B onec \-nt example.nec
.RE
.PP
Process an entire directory tree, four files at a time:
.PP
.RS
.B onec \-r \-j 4 /path/to/models/
.RE
.PP
Process only MMANA-GAL files in a directory tree:
.PP
.RS
.B "onec \-r '/path/to/models/*.maa'"
.RE
.PP
Convert a MMANA-GAL file to NEC format and simulate it:
.PP
.RS
.B onec example.mma
.RE
.PP
Convert a folder of MMANA-GAL files to NEC decks without simulating:
.PP
.RS
.B "onec \-r \-n \-w .nec '/path/to/models/*.mma'"
.RE
.PP
Write a Green's function file alongside the output:
.PP
.RS
.B onec \-g example.nec
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
When a single input file is processed and
.B \-o
is not given, results are written to
.IR stdout .
When multiple files are processed (either by listing them, or with
.BR \-r ),
each file
.I path/to/model.nec
produces a corresponding
.I path/to/model.out
sidecar file, and
.I stdout
is used for per-file progress messages and the end-of-batch summary.
.PP
Errors and warnings always go to
.I stderr
unless redirected with
.BR \-e .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All requested operations completed without error.
.TP
.B 1
One or more errors occurred (parse error, invalid deck, I/O failure).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I *.nec, *.deck
OpenNEC / NEC-2 antenna deck (primary input format).
.TP
.I *.out
Default output file written when processing multiple inputs.
.TP
.I *.ngf
Green's function file written by
.BR \-g .
.SH SEE ALSO
The file
.I doc/OpenNEC file format.md
describes the deck language.
.PP
.I doc/Differences between OpenNEC and nec2c.md
documents behavioural differences from the reference
.BR nec2c (1)
implementation.
.PP
.I doc/YO file format.md
and other files in
.I doc/
cover the supported 3rd-party formats.
.SH HISTORY
OpenNEC is based on the NEC-2 Fortran code released by Lawrence
Livermore National Laboratory in the early 1980s, and on the C port
.BR nec2c
by Neoklis Kyriazis (first released 2003, version 1.3 released 2014).
OpenNEC was forked from nec2c 1.3 and has since been substantially
extended.  Formula evaluation is provided by
.B tinyexpr
by Lewis Van Winkle (zlib licence).
